      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'll bump this now that OSC trackers are a thing.\n\nOSC hand tracking?\n\nPerhaps worthy of a new post.\n\nHm, there is one talking about a hand tracker, but not fingers.\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/add-a-hand-tracker-to-the-osc-tracker\n\nHere it is! Exactly what I'm talking about!\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/add-osc-support-for-handsfingers-please",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-06-01T11:08:16.529Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It is time to bring this back as somehow it seems it is not expressed yet. There are ways in which you can use leap motion in VRC it seems but with much hassle like needing an alternate controller and its finger tracking not being used to its full extent, only the major movements. Leap motion has been around for quite a while now and I feel more users would use it or get it if they just had support in games they play like VRC. As an index user it is nice to be able to adjust where my fingers are, but it still is very limited. With leap motion and its capabilities to track finger movments without controllers, its something that would be fun to use from time to time. Being able to do better gestures, clap probably, take a drink, whatever it is, without the limitations or hassle of controllers. I am sure many alterations of leap motion will be coming out or already are out and I think VRC should be preparing for this future.",
